# exit code: 0 throughout. Every top-level repository entry lands
# directly at the extraction destination — no noye/ wrapper. The
# internal tar member names carry a leading "./" (tar's normal
# behavior for the given source path), which every tested extractor
# (GNU tar here) normalizes away rather than creating a "." directory —
# this is standard tar semantics, not something package.sh does
# specially.

